+# Corpus fetching
+
+## Rate limit actually encountered
+
+The repository does not retain enough fetch telemetry to state the per-domain rate
+limit that this corpus fetch actually encountered. In particular, no fetch script,
+request log, `Retry-After` response, or limiter configuration is present from which
+to recover:
+
+- the number of visits allowed per window;
+- the window length; or
+- the cooldown applied after a breach.
+
+Those values are therefore **unknown**; no numeric limit is asserted here. The only
+contemporaneous description is in `GATE1.md`, which says that fetching was
+rate-limited and performed incrementally.
+
+## Hosts used
+
+- `raw.githubusercontent.com` — the raw-file host used to fetch the corpus files,
+  recorded in the header of `manifest.tsv`.
+
+No other CDN or mirror host used for the corpus fetch is recorded in this checkout.
